ve actually imploded  in collapsed we have about a problem of  corruption we do have that and the only  way to deal with corruption is not to  say that the state should never own  anything to sort out corruption  corruption is not a South African  phenomena it's a phenomenon presidents  or Ramapo stays under pressure to revive  investor competence and boost economic  growth but he has to balance two sides  those who favor encouraging the growth  of private businesses and many  politicians in the ruling ANC party who  are calling for more black economic  empowerment policies including taking  land for redistribution without  compensating the owners her Matassa al  jazeera Johannesburg
 

